# PowerShell scripts are checked out CRLF on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true stores LF in the index while working copies
# may hold either ending. Two files can then differ on disk while `git diff`
# reports nothing, because the index bytes are identical. That happened when
# two PowerShell acceptance scripts used different on-disk endings and a
# byte-identity check went red for a difference no committed content contained.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
